Codex CLI

Install:
  Install missing Codex CLI globally through pnpm; prepare Node.js, pnpm and PATH when installing the CLI.

Upgrade:
  Update the installed Codex CLI through pnpm; prepare Node.js and pnpm as needed.

Status:
  Report the Codex CLI command location and version.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  PNPM_HOME: ~/.local/share/pnpm by default
  Reuse the Node module's saved environment; existing Codex commands satisfy installation.
  Open a new terminal after installation to load PATH changes.
  Run codex to sign in; authentication is managed by Codex.
